## CURRENT STATE

- `frontend/` + `backend/` remain the served product. The public Netlify
  `frontend-next/` beta is separate and is not the Phase 13 cutover.
- Migration numbering is authoritative: Phase 11 = admitted AI extensions,
  Phase 12 = Club/Community, Phase 13 = Cutover.
- Price Intelligence 1A shipped through PR #74. Feature head
  `1b7f93e10bcb859a5e5cd5c0a3384494fa964c99` was squash-merged as
  `f2469958a855ebfc6e37f99bdc292f6c423bb1a8`; the PR contains nine task files
  and excludes `.wslconfig`, which is pre-existing local work.
- Price Intelligence 1A consists of the migration
  `20260824120000_price_intelligence_1a_observations.sql`, a read-only service
  contract/adapter and deterministic adapter tests. It adds no UI, no smart
  price in `/vendi`, no external provider and no paid API.
- `public.wine_price_observations` is append-only and stores integer cents plus
  snapshots of `wine_id` and `formato`. ASKING observations are written only on
  real activation or an active price change; reservation release
  `riservato -> attivo`, same-price changes and metadata-only changes write
  nothing. SALE is written when an order first reaches `completato`; the partial
  unique index on `origine_ref` prevents a second SALE after
  `completato -> contestato -> completato`.
- The public `security_invoker = off` view `public.wine_price_history` exposes
  exactly 11 closed columns and excludes `origine_ref` and personal/domain
  identifiers. `anon` and `authenticated` can SELECT the view but have no base
  table privilege. The base table has RLS enabled and zero client policies.
- Three privileged writer/trigger functions are `SECURITY DEFINER`, have an
  empty `search_path` and no client/service-role EXECUTE ACL. UPDATE, DELETE and
  TRUNCATE are also rejected by append-only triggers even for `service_role`.
- The SQL grid ran on disposable PostgreSQL 17.10 from bootstrap `9c` through
  all 36 migrations: final result **32 PASSA / 0 FALLISCE**, zero fixture
  residue, never production. Cases 31-32 prove the real post-completion dispute
  route does not duplicate SALE.
- Full `frontend-next` verification was green: lint 0 errors / 14 pre-existing
  warnings, typecheck clean, **681 pass / 0 fail** across 46 files and 17,238
  expectation calls, production build green and `git diff --check` clean.
  `MIN_TESTS` is 681 in CI and the prelaunch regression contract.
- PR #74 and post-merge CI run `32734863290` were green for frontend,
  frontend-next and backend. The merge commit's Supabase Preview check was also
  green.
- Production project ref was verified as `pijnmcllmfgjmgsvtcej`. The pre-merge
  PostgREST baseline had 9 active public listings while both new objects were
  absent (404). The post-merge Supabase integration applied only migration
  `20260824120000`; the live ledger now ends at that version.
- Production backfill is **9 ASKING / 0 SALE** for 9 active listings. All nine
  ASKING rows match current `listings.prezzo_cents`; none was imported from
  `prezzo_mercato_cents`. Every row has truthful acquisition timestamp
  `2026-08-24 13:49:02.895298+00`, 35.895298 seconds after the merge timestamp.
- Production catalogs confirm the expected table, enums, five enabled domain
