- The exact production migration ledger was not independently queried before
  merge. The prior verified handoff recorded `20260822000000`; pre-merge 404s
  proved the new objects absent, and the post-merge ledger records
  `20260824120000` with a matching acquisition-time backfill.
- A Supabase CLI dry-run exposed a temporary CLI database credential in local
  command output during verification. It was never committed or documented;
  all temporary credential and schema-dump files were deleted. The credential
  was short-lived CLI material and was not reused after cleanup.
- The grid does not simulate two simultaneous SALE transitions. Concurrency
  safety rests on the live unique partial index, while the grid proves repeated
  and post-dispute transitions serially.
- `wine_price_history` intentionally uses `security_invoker = off`, so the
  Supabase linter's `security_definer_view` signal is expected, as for the other
  public closed-column views.
- Deliberate historical verification residues unrelated to this task remain:
  one test bottle in state `aperta`, the test account, and three objects in each
  of its `cantina` and `annunci` folders.
- Phase 11 implementation is not open. Phase 13 has not started and must not be
  inferred from the public beta, green checks or Price Intelligence 1A.
- External Price Intelligence providers remain OFF and fail-closed. Turning one
  on requires explicit authorization plus a new enum label, CHECK update and
